{%- comment -%}
  A labelled row: a micro label on one side, a display-face value on the other,
  with a hairline under it.

  Two sections wrote this markup independently — craft called its block `spec`
  and visit called its `detail`, and the only difference was that visit's value
  can be a link. Same classes, same structure, same CSS.

  **A row with no value renders nothing**, rather than an empty rule. That is
  visit's rule and it matters there: its rows can draw their value from the
  shop's address, telephone or email, any of which a merchant may not have set.

  **The closing hairline is `.spec-row:last-child`**, so every caller has to
  keep its rows in a wrapper of their own. Render these flat beside anything
  else — a buttons block, say — and the last row stops being the last child,
  the group loses its bottom rule, and whatever follows gains one. craft keeps
  them in `.measure` and visit in a plain `div`; both are deliberate.

  The hero is deliberately not a caller. Its `.hero__choice` looks like a
  labelled row and is not one — it is an art-directed pill sharing a row with
  the metal switch, in the same way `.hero__cta` is not a `.btn`.

  Accepts:
    label      - the micro label
    value      - the value; nothing renders without it
    link       - optional; wraps the value in an anchor
    new_tab    - true to open off-site. The caller works this out
                 (`link contains '://'`) and passes a variable, because a
                 filter cannot be used on a `render` argument.
    attributes - the caller's `block.shopify_attributes`, so the theme editor
                 can still select the row
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if value != blank -%}
  <div class="spec-row" {{ attributes }}>
    <span class="spec-row__label">{{ label }}</span>
    <span class="spec-row__value">
      {%- if link != blank -%}
        <a href="{{ link }}"{% if new_tab %} target="_blank" rel="noopener"{% endif %}>{{ value }}</a>
      {%- else -%}
        {{- value -}}
      {%- endif -%}
    </span>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
